     kkiillll [--ll [_s_i_g_n_a_l]] [--ss _s_i_g_n_a_l] [--_s_i_g_n_a_l] _p_i_d _._._.
         Send a signal, by default SIGTERM, to the process with ID _p_i_d.

         The options to the kkiillll command are as follows:

            --ll [_s_i_g_n_a_l]  List all supported signals, or the signal name corre‐
                         sponding to _s_i_g_n_a_l number or the exit status of a
                         command killed by a signal.
            --ss _s_i_g_n_a_l    Send the process _s_i_g_n_a_l name.
            --_s_i_g_n_a_l      Send the process _s_i_g_n_a_l name or number.
            _p_i_d          A process ID, process group ID, or a job ID (see
